  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 configs (0.715–0.725) all share multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation, with weighted fusion giving the best result (config_001, 0.725). The remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder (scvi_n200) is the bottleneck. Question: config_034 swaps scvi_n200 for scgpt while keeping the best-performing aggregation (transformer) and fusion (weighted) with imagenet_vit_l, directly testing whether a more expressive learned RNA encoder can push accuracy beyond 0.725. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the most targeted extension of the current best configuration, isolating the RNA encoder as the single variable. With 5 experiments remaining, committing to the most promising encoder swap maximizes the chance of finding a new best before budget runs out. Expected cost: ~4–5 GPU hours (scgpt encoder is comparable to or slightly heavier than scvi_n200; transformer aggregation with multiprofile and weighted fusion matches the ~3.6–4.7 h range seen in similar configs), which is acceptable given the potential accuracy gain."
